1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,129
Teacher midterm practice, question 3.

2
00:00:03,749 --> 00:00:07,177
In Figure X, what are the Miller indices of plane C?

3
00:00:07,177 --> 00:00:09,843
Notice that one choice says it is impossible,

4
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:12,836
because the plane extends outside the unit cell.

5
00:00:14,536 --> 00:00:19,337
Read the three intercepts. Plane C meets z at one, at the top of the cube.

6
00:00:19,337 --> 00:00:23,929
It meets y at three halves, outside the cell, and that is perfectly fine.

7
00:00:24,549 --> 00:00:27,425
Along the front edge it has dropped to one half at x

8
00:00:27,425 --> 00:00:30,910
equals one, so it reaches the floor at x equals two.

9
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:34,102
Reciprocals: one half, two thirds, and one.

10
00:00:34,721 --> 00:00:37,239
Multiply by six: three, four, six.

11
00:00:38,839 --> 00:00:41,025
The answer is A: three, four, six.

12
00:00:41,845 --> 00:00:44,877
A plane does not have to fit inside one unit cell.

13
00:00:44,877 --> 00:00:48,654
Only its intercepts matter, and they can be larger than one.
